                            Section("Log-wealth regret",
                                    [Prose("[`log_wealth_regret`](@ref) reads two prediction results scored over the same rows. It returns the difference in log terminal wealth between a comparator and a strategy, the difference row by row, and a Newey-West test that the two have the same expected log growth. The comparator is any prediction result over the rows. It can be the same estimator run causally. It can also be a hindsight comparator, fit on the rows it is scored on and predicted in sample. Through a [`HindsightSplit`](@ref) the comparator changes from row to row, which gives the dynamic regret, and the result reports the path length of the comparator beside the regret. [`BudgetedHindsightPath`](@ref) is the best sequence of comparators whose path length stays within a budget. Its fit solves one programme over the whole panel, and its prediction result has one fold per row. Pass it as the comparator to read the regret at a given budget."),
